node_modules/
# ANCHORED. Unanchored, `out/` matches a directory named `out` at ANY depth — which
# silently swallowed `packages/modules/bridge/src/out/`, the bridge-out SOURCE
# modules, so none of them were ever tracked. Every foundry profile in
# `foundry.toml` writes under the repo-root `out/`, so anchoring loses nothing.
# `cache/` and `broadcast/` stay unanchored on purpose: they DO have legitimate
# nested instances (e.g. `packages/core/cache/`).
/out/
cache/
broadcast/

# Fundraising / positioning material — kept locally, never published with the
# protocol source. Also excluded from the pnpm workspace so a fresh clone (where
# this directory does not exist) still resolves the lockfile cleanly.
packages/pitch-deck/
